The profile's flanks are nearly radial (authored polygonal form): flank slopes run 1–3 mm/deg, so my 0.5 mm/deg "corner" filter discarded 98% of the profile. The samples themselves are smooth. Fix: raise the corner threshold to 50 mm/deg (only true corner spikes), and compute cross-y constancy as a direct same-angle comparison instead of via the noise-dominated folded means:
